1. Introduction
The precipitation and dissolution processes of calcium carbonate are very important in a vast number of scientific areas and relevant research is
relentlessly continuing, since, several aspects contributing to our understanding of these processes remain still unclear. One of the features which is of key importance to the interpretation of phenomena related to precipitation and dissolution processes is the polymorphism of carbonate [1]. The polymorphs which are formed at ambient temperature and in the absence of additives during the
